  "body": "Refs #3522.\n\n## What happens\nThe step \"Batch gate tier\" of `.github/workflows/post-merge.yml` has `timeout-minutes: 45`. The step \"Gate summary\" reads a run of 44 minutes or more as a timeout (`mins -ge 44`).\n\nPR #3363 added the dependency `wgpu` and the crate `camcraft-gpu`. Each runner must build `app`, `gpu` and `ui` from a cold state one time. That build does not complete in 45 minutes:\n- run 45045638947 (deb5364ee) on the runner `egg`: ended in step 08, `debug build: app (--no-run)`;\n- run 45046106061 (87fb95f29) on the runner `cheese`: ended in step 10, `debug build: ui (--no-run)`.\n\nNo test ran in these runs. The issue \"main is red\" (#3522) opened with no FAIL row.\n\n## Wanted (the exact change that the maintainer named)\n- The step limit of \"Batch gate tier\": 45 -> 75 minutes.\n- The check in \"Gate summary\": 44 -> 74.\n- The comment text in the workflow agrees with the new numbers.\n- No other change: the job limit of 90 minutes stays, the 15-minute watchdog of `xtask` for a silent step stays, and no trigger changes.\n",
